From 4c7e23190c441d148cf87d34df32e453228265d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWCH Phase 4 <phase4@openwch.local>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 07:08:02 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] RISC-V: gate finish-time privilege attributes on
 --w_priv_spec

The official WCH 12.2 assembler canonicalizes explicit architecture attributes but does not synthesize Tag_RISCV_priv_spec attributes at finish time after CSR or privileged instructions, unless its hidden --w_priv_spec flag is given. Add that flag, default it off, and gate the synthesis on it. Attributes an input wrote explicitly are unaffected because they are recorded when the directive is parsed, and the inherited tests that expected the upstream-generated tags are updated for the new default.

The flag takes no argument, is accepted with one or two leading dashes through getopt_long_only, is absent from --help, and is idempotent. It is the only factor this patch adds: whether an attribute section is emitted at all still follows the upstream arch_attr/explicit_attr path, and the upstream start_assemble and explicit_priv_attr conditions still decide whether there is a privilege spec to write at all.

WCH 12.2 behavior evidence: tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-attribute-official/ and tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-attribute-final/. Official option surface, including the no-argument diagnostic, the single-dash and abbreviated spellings, the empty --help match and the idempotent object: tmp/phase8-evidence/12.2.0/probes/u1-gas-options.log. Official gate-factor decomposition, including the -mno-arch-attr, empty-file, no-CSR and -mpriv-spec cases and the explicit-attribute quadrant: tmp/phase8-evidence/12.2.0/probes/u1-gas-gate.log and tmp/phase8-evidence/12.2.0/probes/u3-spec-detail.log section 2. Full RISC-V GAS regression evidence: tmp/phase4-evidence/s3-vendor-x-final/.
